Parts of this software are adapted from DeepGSB:

    Deep Generalized Schrödinger Bridge
    Guan-Horng Liu, Tianrong Chen, Oswin So, Evangelos A. Theodorou
    Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, 2022
    https://github.com/ghliu/DeepGSB
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

The following parts of src/nlmfsp/networks.py are derived from that work, with
modifications:

  timestep_embedding
      Adapted from DeepGSB models/util.py. The frequency bands and the
      [cos, sin] concatenation are unchanged. Modified to validate the input
      shape and to require an even embedding dimension.

  ToyValueNet
      Generalizes the ToyY architecture of DeepGSB models/toy_net.py. The
      separate time and space branches, their concatenation and the three-layer
      output head are the same; fixed layer widths were replaced by
      configuration-driven ones, and optional sinusoidal time embedding and time
      normalization were added.

  ToyGradientNet
      Generalizes the ToyZ architecture of DeepGSB models/toy_net.py, in the
      same way. Here the two branches are summed rather than concatenated, and
      the output head has two layers, following the upstream design.

tests/test_toy_networks.py checks that these two networks have the same
parameter counts as the upstream reference under the configuration used in the
paper.

